    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Grading:</h3>
    <p>Your instructor will assign due dates for all and will provide you with detailed assignment sheets that describe expectations, constraints, and deadlines for each project. Students have unlimited submission attempts for each assignment before the deadline. The highest grade will be taken into consideration.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Revisions:</h3>
    <p>A student may revise any major assignment. A revised project will be accepted if it meets the following guidelines: Once the original project is graded and returned, the student will need to meet with their professor through a virtual or physical conference and visit the University Writing Center for feedback. The UWC can provide proof of attendance through physical and email correspondence. ANY PROJECTS NOT ORIGINALLY SUBMITTED FOR A GRADE WILL NOT BE ELIGIBLE FOR REVISION.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Extra Credit:</h3>
    <p>Visiting the UWC can earn students extra credit points! One per assignment (excluding reading responses/discussions), a student can earn 10 extra credit by visiting the writing center. Refer to the University Writing Center section in the syllabus on how to set up a visit.</p>
    <p>Students have the option of earning extra credit if they attend a <span data-field="event_type">{{ event_type }}</span> or another approved event. Rhetoric is not just written words but spoken words as well. Even though we are going through a pandemic, there are various web-based lectures that can be delivered through new technologies and mediums. A 220 word analysis of the performance must be submitted (with proof of attendance) to receive ten (10) extra credit points.</p>

